1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:02,968
B, gamma times greater in magnitude.

2
00:00:02,968 --> 00:00:11,067
The isothermal slope is minus P over V, and the adiabatic slope is minus gamma P over V.

3
00:00:11,067 --> 00:00:17,174
Since gamma is bigger than one, the adiabatic is always the steeper curve.

